BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fluxus-cpga-prize-frieze-london-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260918T215132Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260928
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260929
SUMMARY:Deadline: Fluxus-CPGA Prize at Frieze London 2026
DESCRIPTION:The Fluxus-CPGA Prize at Frieze London\, a collaboration betwee
 n Fluxus Art Projects\, the Comite Professionnel des Galeries d'Art and Fr
 ieze London\, supports talent from the French art scene and promotes its v
 isibility internationally. It also celebrates the relationship between art
 ists and their galleries: the GBP 15\,000 prize is shared between the two.
  WHO APPLIES: galleries of any nationality exhibiting at Frieze London 202
 6\, presenting the work of one French or French-based artist on their stan
 d\; artists cannot apply directly. HOW TO APPLY: via the Google Form linke
 d from the apply page\, with gallery contact information\, the artist's na
 me and number of works presented\, an artist biography (200 words)\, a gal
 lery description (200 words) and 1 to 2 images. Free of charge. Previous l
 aureates include Daiga Grantina (Emalin\, 2025)\, Stephanie Saade (Marfa' 
 Projects\, 2024) and Josefa Ntjam (Nicoletti\, 2023)\; jurors have include
 d Hans Ulrich Obrist\, Zoe Whitley\, Catherine Wood and Valeria Napoleone.
  Deadline 28 September 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Fluxus Art Projects\, with t
 he Comite Professionnel des Galeries d'Art and Frieze London\nLocation: Fr
 ieze London\, Regent's Park\, London\, UK (October 2026). Galleries of any
  nationality can apply\, provided they present the work of a French or Fre
 nch-based artist on their stand.\nAward: GBP 15\,000 prize\, shared betwee
 n the artist and their gallery. Participation is free of charge.\nDuration
 : Awarded during Frieze London in October 2026\n\nMore: https://fluxusartp
 rojects.com/apply?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referra
 l
URL:https://fluxusartprojects.com/apply?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Frieze London\, Regent's Park\, London\, UK (October 2026). Galler
 ies of any nationality can apply\, provided they present the work of a Fre
 nch or French-based artist on their stand.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fluxus-prize-art-basel-paris-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260918T215132Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260929
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260930
SUMMARY:Deadline: Fluxus Prize at Art Basel Paris 2026
DESCRIPTION:The Fluxus Prize at Art Basel Paris\, from Fluxus Art Projects\
 , supports talent from the British art scene and promotes its visibility i
 nternationally\, honouring the relationship between artists and their gall
 eries: the EUR 15\,000 prize is shared between the two. This edition is su
 pported by Belinda de Gaudemar and Laurent Issaurat. WHO APPLIES: gallerie
 s of any nationality exhibiting at Art Basel Paris 2026 in the Galleries o
 r Premise sectors\, presenting the work of one British or UK-based artist\
 ; artists cannot apply directly. HOW TO APPLY: by email to visual.arts[at]
 institut-francais.org.uk with gallery contact information\, the artist's n
 ame and number of works presented\, an artist biography (200 words)\, a ga
 llery description (200 words) and 1 to 2 images. Free of charge. Previous 
 laureates include Olu Ogunnaike (Hollybush Gardens\, 2025) and Jesse Darli
 ng (Sultana\, 2024)\; jurors have included Hans Ulrich Obrist\, Caroline B
 ourgeois and Daria de Beauvais. Deadline 29 September 2026.\n\nOrganisatio
 n: Fluxus Art Projects\, with Art Basel Paris\nLocation: Art Basel Paris\,
  France (October 2026). Galleries of any nationality can apply\, provided 
 they present the work of one British or UK-based artist in the Galleries o
 r Premise sectors.\nAward: EUR 15\,000 prize\, shared between the artist a
 nd their gallery. Participation is free of charge.\nDuration: Awarded duri
 ng Art Basel Paris in October 2026\n\nMore: https://fluxusartprojects.com/
 apply?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://fluxusartprojects.com/apply?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Art Basel Paris\, France (October 2026). Galleries of any national
 ity can apply\, provided they present the work of one British or UK-based 
 artist in the Galleries or Premise sectors.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:script-pipeline-first-look-project-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260918T215132Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: Script Pipeline: First Look Project 2026 (screenplay and 
 TV pilot contest)
DESCRIPTION:The 15th annual First Look Project from Script Pipeline searche
 s for higher-concept material across six categories: feature screenplays i
 n Action and Sci-Fi\, Comedy\, Drama\, and Horror and Thriller\, plus hour
  and half-hour original TV pilots. Unlike Script Pipeline's Screenwriting 
 and TV Writing contests\, entries are judged on both writing ability and m
 arket potential\, in addition to originality of concept\; a script that st
 ill needs refining can win if the story could stand out in the current lan
 dscape\, as the aim is a first look at the next buzzworthy specs before th
 ey hit the market. GUIDELINES: screenplays must be feature length\; genres
  without a listed category go to the closest one (Fantasy\, Western or Adv
 enture under Action and Sci-Fi\; Crime and Mystery under Thriller). TV pil
 ots run roughly 30 to 60 pages\, all genres accepted including animation a
 nd genre hybrids. The script must not be under an option or shopping agree
 ment at the time of entry\, and the same script cannot compete in multiple
  categories. CIRCULATION: Script Pipeline's industry relationships (Bellev
 ue Productions\, LBI Entertainment\, Hungry Man\, Alibi Management and oth
 ers) have led to writers signed\, specs sold and films produced. Regular d
 eadline 30 September 2026\; late deadline 15 October\; extended deadline 3
 0 October. Winners announced 15 December 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Script Pip
 eline\nLocation: Online submission\; open to writers worldwide. Script Pip
 eline is based in Los Angeles\, US.\nAward: USD 15\,000 in total prizes ac
 ross six winners: USD 2\,500 to the winner of each of four screenplay genr
 e categories (Action and Sci-Fi\, Comedy\, Drama\, Horror and Thriller) an
 d USD 2\,500 to the winner of each of two TV pilot categories (hour and ha
 lf-hour). All winners also receive long-term circulation to Script Pipelin
 e's industry network of producers\, managers\, agents and directors\, 1-on
 -1 development assistance from Script Pipeline execs\, additional script r
 eviews and consideration of other material\, career guidance and mentorshi
 p\, and invitations to private Symposium events. Entry fee: USD 60 at the 
 regular deadline\, rising to USD 65 (late\, 15 October) and USD 70 (extend
 ed\, 30 October).\nDuration: Winners announced 15 December 2026.\n\nMore: 
 https://scriptpipeline.com/contest/first-look-project?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://scriptpipeline.com/contest/first-look-project?utm_source=artifi
 cialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online submission\; open to writers worldwide. Script Pipeline is 
 based in Los Angeles\, US.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bigci-environmental-awards-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260918T215132Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260802
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260803
SUMMARY:Deadline: BigCi Environmental Awards 2026
DESCRIPTION:BigCi's Environmental Awards are an annual prize for work that 
 engages with the environment\, open to Australian and international artist
 s working in visual art\, installation\, multimedia\, performance\, litera
 ture\, music\, photography\, filmmaking and curating. TWO WINNERS each rec
 eive four weeks of free residency at BigCi plus AUD 5\,000 in prize money.
  BigCi sits on the edge of Wollemi National Park in the Greater Blue Mount
 ains\, an hour and a half from Sydney but geologically another world\; win
 ners explore the UNESCO World Heritage-listed Wollemi\, Blue Mountains and
  Gardens of Stone National Parks on guided walks and are given research as
 sistance relevant to their projects. At the end of their residencies they 
 present the work at the BigCi Open Day. JUDGING: three independent judges\
 , Lea Kannar-Lichtenberger (Australia)\, Brian Wallace (China) and Dan Got
 tlieb (USA). APPLICATION: an online submission form (Wufoo) linked from th
 e awards page\, with a non-refundable AUD 40 entry fee paid at the time of
  submission. KEY DATES: submissions close 2 August 2026\; winners announce
 d 22 August 2026. Enquiries via the contact form at bigci.org/contact.\n\n
 Organisation: Bilpin International Ground for Creative Initiatives (BigCi)
 \nLocation: Bilpin\, New South Wales\, Australia\, on the edge of Wollemi 
 National Park in the UNESCO World Heritage-listed Greater Blue Mountains\,
  about 1.5 hours from Sydney. Open to Australian and international artists
 .\nAward: Two awards\, each of AUD 5\,000 prize money plus four weeks of f
 ree residency at BigCi\, guided walks in the surrounding national parks an
 d research assistance for the project. AUD 40 entry fee\, non-refundable a
 nd payable with the submission.\nDuration: Four-week residency at BigCi pe
 r winner\n\nMore: https://bigci.org/awards/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://bigci.org/awards/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Bilpin\, New South Wales\, Australia\, on the edge of Wollemi Nati
 onal Park in the UNESCO World Heritage-listed Greater Blue Mountains\, abo
 ut 1.5 hours from Sydney. Open to Australian and international artists.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:inlaks-fine-art-award-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260918T215132Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260816
SUMMARY:Deadline: Inlaks Shivdasani Foundation: Inlaks Fine Art Award 2027
DESCRIPTION:A one-year award enabling an emerging Indian visual artist to p
 ursue independent practice\, with a stipulation to attend a recognised art
  residency programme in India for four weeks during the year. ELIGIBILITY 
 IS RESTRICTED: Indian citizens currently living in India\, born on or afte
 r 1 January 1996\, who are either recent graduates\, postgraduates or fina
 l-year students of a leading Indian visual arts institute\, or artists wit
 hout those formal credentials but with a record of exhibition participatio
 n. First-year MA students are not eligible. Awardees submit progress repor
 ts at six months and on completion\, plus documentation of the residency. 
 Applications close 15 August 2026 at 23:59 IST via Submittable. Shortlisti
 ng is expected in late October 2026 with interviews in early November.\n\n
 Organisation: Inlaks Shivdasani Foundation\nLocation: India. Open to India
 n citizens currently living in India.\nAward: INR 300\,000 (around USD 3\,
 400 / EUR 2\,950) for one year\, plus a fully covered four-week art reside
 ncy at an Indian art institution. No application fee.\nDuration: Twelve mo
 nths of independent practice\, including a mandatory four-week residency w
 ithin India.\n\nMore: https://inlaksfoundation.submittable.com/submit/75e1
 4093-df9b-41c5-af96-ce2360e64e1b/the-inlaks-fine-art-award-2027?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://inlaksfoundation.submittable.com/submit/75e14093-df9b-41c5-af96
 -ce2360e64e1b/the-inlaks-fine-art-award-2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:India. Open to Indian citizens currently living in India.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:inlaks-theatre-award-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260918T215132Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260816
SUMMARY:Deadline: Inlaks Shivdasani Foundation: Inlaks Theatre Art Award 20
 27
DESCRIPTION:A skill-enhancement award for emerging Indian theatre practitio
 ners\, supporting participation in recognised training workshops\, residen
 cies and similar programmes rather than the production of a specific work.
  ELIGIBILITY IS RESTRICTED: Indian citizens born after 1 January 1991\, wi
 th preference given to holders of a theatre degree from a leading Indian i
 nstitution. Recipients report at the six-month mark and on completion. App
 lications close 15 August 2026 at 23:59 IST via Submittable. The foundatio
 n runs several other awards on adjacent deadlines\, including the Inlaks-A
 ttakkalari Dance Studentship (30 August 2026) and a two-month Inlaks Resid
 ency at the International Center of Photography in the USA for emerging In
 dian photographic practitioners (31 August 2026).\n\nOrganisation: Inlaks 
 Shivdasani Foundation\nLocation: India. Open to Indian citizens.\nAward: I
 NR 15\,000 per month for up to 12 months\, around INR 180\,000 total (roug
 hly USD 2\,050 / EUR 1\,780). No application fee.\nDuration: Up to twelve 
 months of skill enhancement\, with six-month interim and final reporting.\
 n\nMore: https://www.inlaksfoundation.org/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.inlaksfoundation.org/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:India. Open to Indian citizens.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bloomberg-green-docs-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260918T215132Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260815
SUMMARY:Deadline: Bloomberg Green Docs Competition 2026 (Short Climate Docu
 mentary)
DESCRIPTION:The Bloomberg Green Docs competition is open to all eligible fi
 lmmakers competing for a $25\,000 grand prize for a short climate document
 ary. The call seeks films that explore our climate future and reveal the w
 orld we are making today: ecosystems being restored\, tomorrow's zero-carb
 on communities being formed\, and habitat extremes warning of cascading cl
 imate consequences. REQUIREMENTS: films must address the urgency of climat
 e change and run under 10 minutes including credits. The jury awards a $25
 \,000 grand prize\, announced at the Bloomberg Green Docs Film Festival in
  New York City on 22 September 2026\, where the top five documentaries wil
 l be screened. Check the official rules on the competition site for eligib
 ility details. DEADLINE: submissions accepted through 14 August 2026.\n\nO
 rganisation: Bloomberg Green\nLocation: Open call for filmmakers (see elig
 ibility rules on the site)\; festival screening in New York City\, USA.\nA
 ward: $25\,000 grand prize awarded by a jury\; the top five documentaries 
 screen at the Bloomberg Green Docs Film Festival in New York City. No entr
 y fee stated.\nDuration: Winner announced at the festival on 22 September 
 2026\n\nMore: https://www.bloomberg.com/greendocs/?utm_source=artificialno
 uveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.bloomberg.com/greendocs/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Open call for filmmakers (see eligibility rules on the site)\; fes
 tival screening in New York City\, USA.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:new-emergence-art-prize-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260918T215132Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260803
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260804
SUMMARY:Deadline: New Emergence Art Prize 2026
DESCRIPTION:The New Emergence Art Prize 2026 is an international open call 
 for emerging artists\, presented by New Emergence Art. There is no set the
 me and work may be submitted in any medium. AWARDS: a prize fund worth ove
 r GBP 5\,000 across nine awards supporting artists through cash prizes\, a
 rtist materials\, mentoring\, and a residency\, including a GBP 1\,000 Gra
 nd Prize\, a two-week NG Art Creative Residency in Provence\, France (wort
 h EUR 2\,000)\, a GBP 300 Founder's Prize cash award\, and materials or su
 bscription awards from Staedtler UK\, Rosemary & Co\, GreatArt\, Michael H
 arding\, and The Art Ladder. ELIGIBILITY: open internationally to emerging
  artists\; entrants may submit up to three original artworks that represen
 t the quality\, originality and direction of their practice. Final selecti
 ons are made by an independent judging panel considering concept\, executi
 on\, originality and impact. Shortlisted artists are featured in an online
  exhibition running 11 August to 7 September 2026. NOTE: there is a paid e
 ntry fee (amount set at the entry step). DEADLINE: 3 August 2026\, 23:59 B
 ST. Apply via https://www.newemergenceart.com/apply.\n\nOrganisation: New 
 Emergence Art\nLocation: International\; open worldwide. Shortlist shown i
 n an online exhibition.\nAward: Prize fund worth over GBP 5\,000 across ni
 ne awards\, including a GBP 1\,000 Grand Prize cash award\, a two-week NG 
 Art Creative Residency in Provence\, France (worth EUR 2\,000)\, a GBP 300
  Founder's Prize cash award\, and materials or subscription awards from St
 aedtler UK\, Rosemary & Co\, GreatArt\, Michael Harding\, and The Art Ladd
 er. NOTE: there is a paid entry fee.\nDuration: One-off prize\; shortliste
 d artists shown in an online exhibition 11 August to 7 September 2026\n\nM
 ore: https://www.newemergenceart.com/apply?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.newemergenceart.com/apply?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:International\; open worldwide. Shortlist shown in an online exhib
 ition.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:day-job-short-film-fund-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260918T215132Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260810
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260811
SUMMARY:Deadline: Day Job: Short Film Fund 2026
DESCRIPTION:Short film competition from Day Job Films created to give auteu
 r directors full creative freedom\, awarding a production budget of up to 
 GBP 7\,000 to make a short film with no producer interference or commercia
 l agenda. Open to animation\, live-action and documentary projects. Runs i
 n three rounds: (1) a pitch deck outlining concept\, story\, key character
 s and visual style\; (2) a full script for those who progress\; and (3) an
  interview to discuss the vision and execution. A panel of industry profes
 sionals judges the pitch deck\, script and interview\, with at least one t
 eam member reading each pitch deck and script in full. The winner receives
  full creative control over the project. ELIGIBILITY: applicants can be fr
 om anywhere worldwide\, but all production must take place in the UK\; app
 licants must have a producer on board who is separate from the director/wr
 iter. Applicants may optionally include a plan for adapting the script int
 o a feature-length film (this does not affect the outcome). Submissions op
 en February 10\, 2026 and close August 10\, 2026. Enquiries: hello@dayjobf
 ilms.com.\n\nOrganisation: Day Job Films\nLocation: Worldwide applicants\;
  all production must take place in the UK\nAward: Production budget of up 
 to GBP 7\,000\, with full creative control and no producer or external int
 erference. No application fee.\nDuration: Per short film project\n\nMore: 
 https://www.dayjobfilms.com/short-film-fund?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.dayjobfilms.com/short-film-fund?utm_source=artificialnouvea
 ugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Worldwide applicants\; all production must take place in the UK
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:vh-award-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260918T215132Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260721
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260722
SUMMARY:Deadline: VH AWARD 2026 (Hyundai Motor Group)
DESCRIPTION:The VH AWARD\, hosted by Hyundai Motor Group\, supports emergin
 g media artists whose work engages with the context of Asia\, through an o
 nline residency and exhibitions across global platforms. FIELD: audiovisua
 l\, screen-based artworks including video art\, motion graphics\, animatio
 n\, games\, films or newly explored areas\; proposals must suit single-cha
 nnel video presentation (no interactivity). ELIGIBILITY: individuals or co
 llectives whose work engages with the context of Asia\, including artists 
 of Asian descent\, those based in Asia\, and the Asian diaspora. Five fina
 lists are selected\, each receiving a USD 30\,000 production grant and a p
 lace in the Ars Electronica online residency program (masterclasses and 1:
 1 mentoring)\, with networking and exhibition opportunities\; one Grand Pr
 ix recipient (announced 2027) receives an additional USD 30\,000\; a new H
 onorary Mention category recognises one or two further applicants with web
 site features and selected residency components. APPLY: via the VH AWARD w
 ebsite Entry Portal with a video portfolio (max 3 min)\, CV and artist sta
 tement (max 3 pages)\, and a new artwork proposal (max 3 pages) with a ref
 erence video (max 1 min)\; all documents in English\; proposed works must 
 be original and unexhibited. Open call 26 May - 21 July 2026 (KST)\; final
 ists announced September 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Hyundai Motor Group\nLocat
 ion: Online residency (global exhibitions)\; for artists engaging with Asi
 a\nAward: Each of five finalists receives a USD 30\,000 production grant p
 lus an Ars Electronica online residency\; the Grand Prix winner receives a
 n additional USD 30\,000 (USD 60\,000 total). Honorary Mentions join selec
 ted residency components. No application fee.\nDuration: Online residency 
 Sep 2026 - Mar 2027 (finalists)\; award ceremony and exhibitions June 2027
 \n\nMore: https://vhaward.com/about/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral#entry
URL:https://vhaward.com/about/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_me
 dium=referral#entry
LOCATION:Online residency (global exhibitions)\; for artists engaging with 
 Asia
END:VEVENT
