SUMMARY:Deadline: Simone Veil Prize for European Jewish Cultural Heritage 2
 026
DESCRIPTION:The Simone Veil Prize\, administered by the European Commission
 \, recognises outstanding projects preserving and promoting European Jewis
 h cultural heritage. It is awarded across five categories: Shared Historie
 s\, Heritage for Dialogue\, Living Heritage\, Cross-border Cooperation and
  Shared Narratives\, and Next Generation/Youth Engagement and Education. A
 WARD: €10\,000 per Grand Prix winner (one per category\, five in total)\
 ; up to 25 finalists receive recognition. ELIGIBILITY: legal or natural pe
 rsons (individuals or organisations) registered in EU Member States or thi
 rd countries associated to the Creative Europe programme\; projects must h
 ave been completed between January 2023 and January 2026. DEADLINE: 31 Jul
 y 2026 at 23:59 CET. APPLY by submitting the completed application form by
  email to applications@simoneveilprize.eu.\n\nOrganisation: European Commi
 ssion\, Directorate-General for Education\, Youth\, Sport and Culture\nLoc
 ation: EU Member States and third countries associated to the Creative Eur
 ope programme\nAward: €10\,000 per Grand Prix winner (five winners\, one
  per category)\; up to 25 finalists recognized. No application fee.\nDurat
 ion: For projects completed between January 2023 and January 2026\n\nMore:
  https://simoneveilprize.eu/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
URL:https://simoneveilprize.eu/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_m
 edium=referral
LOCATION:EU Member States and third countries associated to the Creative Eu
 rope programme
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:lee-ufan-arles-art-environment-prize-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260918T215132Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260731
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260801
SUMMARY:Deadline: Lee Ufan Arles: Prix Art & Environnement 2026 (Residency 
 + Exhibition Prize)
DESCRIPTION:The Prix Art & Environnement (4th edition)\, awarded by Lee Ufa
 n Arles and Maison Guerlain\, supports an artist working at the intersecti
 on of art and the natural environment. The prize winner receives a funded 
 6–8 week production residency in Arles in early 2027\, including product
 ion space\, accommodation\, and mentorship from Lee Ufan Arles staff\, cul
 minating in a solo summer 2027 exhibition. ELIGIBILITY: open to all artist
 s of any discipline and nationality\, with no age or degree requirements\;
  candidates must demonstrate at least one solo exhibition and one or more 
 group exhibitions. DEADLINE: 31 July 2026. APPLY via the Google Form linke
 d from the Lee Ufan Arles website.\n\nOrganisation: Lee Ufan Arles and Mai
 son Guerlain\nLocation: Arles\, France (residency and exhibition)\nAward: 
 Funded residency (production space + accommodation) in Arles. No cash priz
 e amount specified. No application fee.\nDuration: 6–8 weeks residency i
 n early 2027\, followed by a solo summer 2027 exhibition\n\nMore: https://
 en.leeufan-arles.org/evenements/art-environment-prize?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://en.leeufan-arles.org/evenements/art-environment-prize?utm_sourc
 e=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Arles\, France (residency and exhibition)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:future-vision-xprize-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260918T215132Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260816
SUMMARY:Deadline: Future Vision XPRIZE (sci-fi film competition)
DESCRIPTION:Future Vision XPRIZE is a sci-fi film competition challenging f
 ilmmakers to portray an optimistic\, abundant future for humanity rather t
 han a dystopian one. CHALLENGE: create a 3-minute sci-fi trailer that depi
 cts a bold\, original\, hopeful vision of progress. PRIZES: USD 3.5 millio
 n-plus total\; the grand prize winner gets USD 2.6 million-plus to turn th
 eir trailer into a feature film\, plus over USD 1 million in prizes for ru
 nners-up. BACKGROUND: launched by the nonprofit XPRIZE and funded by Peter
  Diamandis\, with Google and Range as partners\; inspired by the optimism 
 of Star Trek and intended to give storytellers a hopeful 'north star' for 
 builders. ELIGIBILITY: open to all filmmakers globally. TIMELINE: competit
 ion launched 9 March 2026\; submission deadline 15 August 2026\; finals on
  25 September 2026 in Los Angeles (finalists attend in person). APPLY: reg
 ister and read the rules on the contest website at futurevisionxprize.com.
 \n\nOrganisation: XPRIZE (Future Vision XPRIZE\, funded by Peter Diamandis
 \; partners Google and Range)\nLocation: Online / Worldwide (finals held i
 n Los Angeles)\nAward: USD 3.5 million-plus prize pool. Grand prize winner
  receives USD 2.6 million-plus to develop their vision into a feature film
 \, with over USD 1 million in additional prizes for runners-up.\nDuration:
  One-off competition\; create a 3-minute sci-fi trailer\n\nMore: https://f
 uturevisionxprize.com/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=re
 ferral
URL:https://futurevisionxprize.com/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online / Worldwide (finals held in Los Angeles)
END:VEVENT
